/* book Worked example: Q: An RC low-pass filter has R=1 kΩ and C=1 μF; the output is the capacitor voltage. Find the time constant τ, the impulse response h(t), the step response s(t), and the values of h and s at t=1 ms.
   1. τ=RC=(1×103 Ω)(1×10−6 F)=1×10−3 s=1 ms.
   2. h(t)=(1/τ)e−t/τu(t)=(1/0.001)e−t/0.001u(t)=1000e−1000tu(t) s−1.
   3. s(t)=∫0t1000e−1000λdλ=[−e−1000λ]0t=1−e−1000t for t≥0, so s(t)=(1−e−1000t)u(t).
   4. At t=1 ms, 1000t=1 and e−1=0.3679. So h(1 ms)=1000×0.3679=367.9 s−1, about 368 s−1.
   5. s(1 ms)=1−0.3679=0.632.
   6. Check: ds/dt=1000e−1000t, which is h(t); and s(∞)=1 equals the area under h, 1000×(1/1000)=1.
   Answer: τ=1 ms; h(t)=1000e−1000tu(t) s−1; s(t)=(1−e−1000t)u(t); at t=1 ms, h≈368 s−1 and s=0.632. */
